Apache Mahout is a distributed linear algebra framework.  Its Scala DSL,
"Samsara", is designed to look like the mathematical notation it implements
and lets statisticians and data scientists express their own algorithms,
which Mahout then executes on a distributed back end.

Mahout provides in-core vectors and matrices, distributed row matrices
(DRMs), decompositions (SSVD, thin QR, eigen-, Cholesky), pre-canned
algorithms such as naive Bayes and co-occurrence recommenders, and
automatic optimisation of the algebraic expressions it is given.

This release is used either from its interactive shell or as a library on
a Spark cluster; the MapReduce algorithms and command line drivers of
earlier releases have been removed upstream.
